# Backend Training – Trainer Playbook

## 1. Before starting the program

The trainer must:

- Identify all participants.
- Conduct the initial assessment.
- Record individual strengths and weaknesses.
- Create a dedicated training repository.
- Prepare the development environment.
- Share the training roadmap and SOP.
- Establish assignment submission and review procedures.

## 2. How to handle participants with mixed knowledge

Do not teach everyone at the same speed simply because they attend the same session.

Use three learning tracks:

| Track | Approach |
|---|---|
| Foundation | Complete explanations, demonstrations and guided exercises |
| Intermediate | Short explanations and additional implementation exercises |
| Advanced | Architecture discussions, debugging exercises and more challenging assignments |

All tracks follow the same core curriculum and final assessment.

A participant can move between tracks based on demonstrated competency.

## 3. Trainer preparation checklist

Before every session:

- [ ] Review the session objectives.
- [ ] Prepare the explanation and examples.
- [ ] Prepare a working NestJS demonstration.
- [ ] Prepare the practical exercise.
- [ ] Identify common mistakes.
- [ ] Prepare the assignment.
- [ ] Review previous assignment submissions.

## 4. Session completion checklist

After every session:

- [ ] Mark attendance.
- [ ] Record the topics covered.
- [ ] Record questions and knowledge gaps.
- [ ] Share assignment instructions.
- [ ] Record assignment submission status.
- [ ] Provide feedback.
- [ ] Decide whether revision is necessary.

## 5. Weekly review

At the end of each five sessions:

1. Review completed topics.
2. Conduct a short knowledge assessment.
3. Review practical assignments.
4. Identify participants who need additional guidance.
5. Decide whether the next module can begin.
6. Update individual progress.

