# Backend Training – Participant Handbook

## 1. Participant expectations

Every participant is expected to:

- Attend scheduled training sessions.
- Ask questions when concepts are unclear.
- Complete assigned exercises.
- Practice independently.
- Read and follow the backend SOP.
- Understand the code they submit.
- Participate in code reviews.
- Accept and implement technical feedback.

## 2. Learning expectations

Participants should not focus only on memorizing NestJS decorators or commands.

They should understand:

- Why a particular architecture is used.
- Why a particular database structure is required.
- How requests travel through the application.
- Where business logic should be implemented.
- How errors should be handled.
- How to protect application data.
- How to test their implementation.

## 3. Assignment submission requirements

Every assignment should contain:

1. Source code.
2. Description of implementation.
3. API endpoints implemented.
4. Database changes, if applicable.
5. Tests written.
6. Instructions to run and verify.
7. Known limitations.

## 4. Definition of a completed assignment

An assignment is complete only when:

- Requirements are implemented.
- Code follows the project conventions.
- Relevant tests pass.
- The participant can explain the implementation.
- Reviewer feedback is addressed.

## 5. Learning resources

Use official documentation as the primary reference:

- NestJS: https://docs.nestjs.com/
- TypeScript: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/
- Node.js: https://nodejs.org/en/learn
- PostgreSQL: https://www.postgresql.org/docs/
- Prisma: https://www.prisma.io/docs
- Jest: https://jestjs.io/docs/getting-started
- Fastify: https://fastify.dev/docs/latest/

AI tools may be used for learning and assistance, but participants must understand, verify and take responsibility for the code they submit.